"""Mutants on the lines SPEC 0.3 to 0.16 and 0.18 added (apc_block.py, apc_verify.py, apc_batch.py, apc_l1proof.py, apc_svm.py,
apc_solana.py, apc_report.py, apc_mcp.py, apc_ap2.py, apc_http.py, apc_permit2.py, apc_registry.py, apc_offer.py,
apc_builder.py, apc_payid.py, apc_transport.py, apc_drafts.py, apc_intl.py, apc_assets.py, apc_stellar.py, apc_xlm.py,
apc_v1.py, apc_drafts2.py, apc_drafts3.py, apc_dr3783.py, apc_authcap.py, apc_xrp.py, apc_xrpl.py; and tools/regress.py,
tools/make_bundles_negatives.py, tools/scan_negatives_evm.py, tools/fuzz_bundles.py, tools/equiv_x04.py,
tools/equiv_r02.py, tools/equiv_mutants.py). Each mutant is
applied to a temporary copy (HOME isolated, APC_SIGLIB and
APC_PULSE_CASES kept) and tools/run_ordered.py runs the test modules of its MODS on it. 'killed' = the tests
exit 1 and unittest names a failing test (FAIL: or ERROR: line); exit 0 = SURVIVED; any other exit = INVALID, not
killed. The unmutated copy must pass first (positive control of the bench); a pattern found 0 or 2+ times is STALE.

  python3 tools/mutants03.py ROOT [NAME_SUBSTRING] [i/n]

With env APC_MUT_JOURNAL=FILE every outcome (control and each mutant) is appended to FILE by tools/bench_journal.py,
hash-chained and fsync'ed, bound to the digest of ROOT, of the two input files or trees, the Python version and the
arguments; a run stopped by a machine stop is resumed by running the same command again: what FILE records is not run
again, and FILE under another binding is a refusal (exit 3). tools/bench_cert.py checks the journals of a bench.
"""
